Example Solidity contracts with their compiled artifacts and Go bindings, used by
Go tests of the Paxeer X chain (for example modules/evm, rpc and engine tests).

Directories: echo, erc1155, erc20, erc2981, erc721, sendall, simplestorage.
Each holds the .sol source, the .abi and .bin produced by solc, and, where the
tests use one, a Go binding produced by abigen.

Tools: solc (Solidity compiler) and abigen (the go-ethereum binding generator).

Regenerate an example from the repository root (simplestorage as the example):

solc --overwrite --bin -o example/contracts/simplestorage example/contracts/simplestorage/SimpleStorage.sol
solc --overwrite --abi -o example/contracts/simplestorage example/contracts/simplestorage/SimpleStorage.sol
abigen --abi=example/contracts/simplestorage/SimpleStorage.abi --pkg=simplestorage --out=example/contracts/simplestorage/SimpleStorage.go

The pointer contract artifacts under modules/evm/artifacts are regenerated from
contracts/src; see modules/evm/artifacts/README.
